.TH std::mdspan::mapping-traits 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::mdspan::mapping-traits \- std::mdspan::mapping-traits

.SH Synopsis
constexpr bool is_unique() const;             \fB(1)\fP (since C++23)
constexpr bool is_exhaustive() const;         \fB(2)\fP (since C++23)
constexpr bool is_strided() const;            \fB(3)\fP (since C++23)
static constexpr bool is_always_unique();     \fB(4)\fP (since C++23)
static constexpr bool is_always_exhaustive(); \fB(5)\fP (since C++23)
static constexpr bool is_always_strided();    \fB(6)\fP (since C++23)

Checks if (1-3) the underlying layout mapping map_ or (4-6) its type mapping_type models
the semantics of LayoutMapping's predicate mapping traits.

1-3) Let func be \fB(1)\fP is_unique, \fB(2)\fP is_exhaustive, or \fB(3)\fP is_strided, then it's equivalent
to return map_.func();.
4-6) Let func be \fB(4)\fP is_always_unique, \fB(5)\fP is_always_exhaustive, or \fB(6)\fP is_always_strided,
then it's equivalent to return mapping_type::func();.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

See above.

